    "notes": ["Header order: the official NodeMCU DevKit v1.0 pin definition image (antenna at the top); the schematic's J1/J2 agree and the repo's board photo shows it is the top view (NODEMCU-PINMAP)(NODEMCU-SCH)(NODEMCU-REPO)","USB-serial chip is a Silicon Labs CP2102; 3.3 V comes from an NCP1117 (1 A) regulator (NODEMCU-SCH)","Blue LED (LED1) runs from 3.3 V through 470 ohm into GPIO16/D0, so it lights when D0 is low (NODEMCU-SCH)","The pin map calls the pin under A0 'reserved', but the schematic connects it to the raw ADC node (after the 220k/100k divider). Leave it unconnected (NODEMCU-SCH)(NODEMCU-PINMAP)","To flash by hand: hold FLASH and press RST once (NODEMCU-REPO)","Deep-sleep wake needs D0 (GPIO16) joined to RST (NODEMCU-SCH)","Boot straps: GPIO0 (D3), GPIO2 (D4) and GPIO15 (D8). Normal run: D3 high, D4 high, D8 low; download: D3 low (ESP8266-DS)(ESP01S-SPEC)","All I/O is 3.3 V: input high must not exceed 3.6 V (ESP8266-DS)","D0 (GPIO16) is plain GPIO only: no interrupt, PWM, I2C or one-wire (NODEMCU-PINMAP)","'LoLin V3' is LoLin's own name, not a NodeMCU release. Its layout differs only in the two RSV pins: one is USB 5 V out, the other an extra GND (the source does not say which, so read the printed labels). It is much wider than this board (FRIGHTANIC)"],
