    "notes": ["Header order: Espressif's J2/J3 tables (pin 1 at the antenna end), placed with Espressif's pin layout image (J2 left, J3 right) (DEVKITC-UG)(DEVKITC-PINLAYOUT)","Power from one source only: USB, or the 5V and GND pins, or the 3V3 and GND pins; more than one can damage the board or the supply (DEVKITC-UG)","Download mode: hold Boot, then press EN (DEVKITC-UG)","D0-D3, CMD and CLK go to the SPI flash: do not use them. On WROOM-32E modules GPIO6-11 are not brought out of the module at all (DEVKITC-UG)(WROOM32E-DS)","GPIO16/17 are free only on WROOM and SOLO-1 boards; WROVER boards use them internally, and WROOM-32E/32UE '...R2' modules (PSRAM in package) use GPIO16 (DEVKITC-UG)(WROOM32E-DS)","GPIO34-39 (VP, VN, IO34, IO35) are input only, with no pull-ups or pull-downs (ESP32-DS)","Strapping pins: GPIO0, GPIO2, GPIO5, GPIO12 (MTDI) and GPIO15 (MTDO). IO12 must be low at power-on (ESP32-DS)(WROOM32E-DS)","ADC2 is shared with Wi-Fi, so ADC2 reads can fail while Wi-Fi runs; prefer ADC1 pins. On this board GPIO0 also cannot be read in ADC oneshot mode (auto-flash circuit) (IDF-ADC)","Input high max is VDD + 0.3 V (about 3.6 V): no 5 V on any GPIO (ESP32-DS)","Early V4 boards: capacitor C15 can make the board start in download mode; remove C15 if that happens (DEVKITC-UG)","The only LED Espressif lists is the 5 V power LED (DEVKITC-UG)"],
