    "notes": ["Header order: SparkFun's Pro Mini graphical datasheet (chip side up, FTDI header at the top) (SFE-PROMINI-GDS)","Side rows and programming header are from SparkFun's own Pro Mini (SparkFun designs and makes the Arduino Pro Mini) (SFE-PROMINI-GDS)(ARD-PROMINI)","A4 (SDA), A5 (SCL), A6 and A7 are not on the edge rows: they are four inner holes beside the right-hand row (chip side up, programming header at the top; read from the back-of-board photo), labelled A6 A7 A4 A5 on the back. From the header end they run A5, A4, then A7, A6. Draw them as an inset; clones place them differently, so check the back silkscreen. (SFE-PROMINI-GDS)(SFE-PROMINI-GUIDE)","A6 and A7 have no digital pin number in SparkFun's datasheet: analog input only (SFE-PROMINI-GDS)","Clones differ: some have A4/A5 offset or in line with the edge pins, A6/A7 swapped, the programming header reversed, VCC/GND swapped at the A6/A7 end, or a double row at that end. Read your own board's silkscreen before wiring the end and inner pins (ARD-FORUM-PROMINI)","One clone seller's board puts A4/A5 inside, offset from A2/A3, and A6/A7 on the end of the board (PROTO-PROMINI)","No USB on board: program it with a USB-serial adapter on the 6-pin header (choose 'Arduino Pro or Pro Mini' and the processor that matches: 'ATmega328P (5V, 16 MHz)' or 'ATmega328P (3.3V, 8 MHz)') (ARD-PROMINI)(ARD-AVR-BOARDS)","Raw input: 5 V/16 MHz board 5-16 V (6-12 V recommended); 3.3 V/8 MHz board 3.3-16 V (4-12 V recommended); up to 150 mA from VCC. Arduino's page says up to 12 V (SFE-PROMINI-GDS)(SFE-PROMINI-GDS-3V3)(ARD-PROMINI)","A 5 V clone seller recommends 6-12 V on RAW and rates only 25 mA from the VCC pin, against SparkFun's 150 mA (PROTO-PROMINI)(SFE-PROMINI-GDS)","Never feed different voltages into RAW and VCC at the same time (PROTO-PROMINI)","The 3.3 V version runs its I/O at 3.3 V: 5 V-only parts may need level shifting, and the USB-serial adapter's logic level must match the board (some FTDI boards have a 3.3 V / 5 V jumper) (SFE-PROMINI-GUIDE)","Built-in LED on D13 (green on SparkFun boards); red LED is power (ARD-PROMINI)(SFE-PROMINI-GDS)","Older boards used the ATmega168 (pick the ATmega168 processor entry for those) (ARD-PROMINI)(ARD-AVR-BOARDS)"],
    "sources": [{"title":"SFE-PROMINI-GDS: SparkFun, Arduino Pro Mini 5V/16MHz graphical datasheet (DEV-11113)","url":"https://cdn.sparkfun.com/assets/d/5/2/f/0/ProMini16MHzv2.pdf"},{"title":"SFE-PROMINI-GDS-3V3: SparkFun, Arduino Pro Mini 3.3V/8MHz graphical datasheet (DEV-11114)","url":"https://cdn.sparkfun.com/assets/c/6/2/2/1/ProMini8MHzv2.pdf"},{"title":"SFE-PROMINI-GUIDE: SparkFun, Using the Arduino Pro Mini 3.3V","url":"https://learn.sparkfun.com/tutorials/using-the-arduino-pro-mini-33v/all"},{"title":"ARD-PROMINI: Arduino, Arduino Pro Mini (retired board page, docs-content source)","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/arduino/docs-content/main/content/retired/01.boards/arduino-pro-mini/content.md"},{"title":"ARD-AVR-BOARDS: Arduino, ArduinoCore-avr boards.txt (Nano and Pro Mini processor menus)","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/arduino/ArduinoCore-avr/master/boards.txt"},{"title":"ARD-FORUM-PROMINI: Arduino Forum, Arduino Pro Mini - How many varieties?","url":"https://forum.arduino.cc/t/arduino-pro-mini-how-many-varieties/462274"},{"title":"PROTO-PROMINI: ProtoSupplies, Pro Mini 5V 16MHz Arduino Compatible (clone)","url":"https://protosupplies.com/product/pro-mini-5v-16mhz-arduino-compatible/"}],
