    "notes": ["Header order: the lgt8fx Nano-style pinout diagram (USB at the bottom), checked against its CSV and board photo (LGT8FX-NANO-PINOUT)(LGT8FX-NANO-CSV)(LGT8FX-NANO-PHOTO)","Long-side pin names and positions match the Arduino Nano (drawn here with USB at the bottom, so sides and order are rotated from the Nano entry) (WOLLE-MINIEVB)(LGT8FX-NANO-PINOUT)","Green board: Micro-USB, no crystal, Holtek HT42B534 USB-serial. Purple board: USB-C, 16 MHz crystal, CH9340C USB-serial. Pinouts are similar (WOLLE-MINIEVB)(LGT8FX-WIKI-NANO)","Not a real ATmega328P: install the lgt8fx board package and pick board 'LGT8F328' with the 328P-LQFP32 variant, not 'Arduino Nano' (LGT8FX-README)(WOLLE-LGT)","Bare chips are not programmed over SPI/ICSP: use the SWC/SWD pins with LarduinoISP (an LGT Nano can act as the programmer, though the purple USB-C board would not in Wolle's tests) and 'Burn Bootloader' to restore USB uploads (WOLLE-LGT)(WOLLE-MINIEVB)","Runs up to 32 MHz from its internal 32 MHz oscillator (ATmega328P: 20 MHz max, 8 MHz internal) (WOLLE-LGT)","EEPROM is emulated in flash: 1 KB of EEPROM uses 2 KB of flash (WOLLE-LGT)","ADC: up to 12 bit, internal references 1.024 / 2.048 / 4.096 V, differential inputs with x1/x8/x16/x32 gain (WOLLE-LGT)","Real 8-bit DAC output on D4 (DAC0) (WOLLE-LGT)(LGT8FX-VARIANT)","I/O current up to 30 mA per pin (ATmega328P: 40 mA); TX, D2, D5 and D6 can drive 80 mA after the HDR register is set (WOLLE-LGT)","PWM on 3, 5, 6, 9, 10, 11 as on the 328P, plus D1 and D2 through timer 3; D8 is not a PWM pin even though some diagrams mark it (WOLLE-LGT)","A6, A7, REF, SWC and SWD also work as digital pins (on a real Nano A6/A7 are analog only) (WOLLE-MINIEVB)","RST can be made an I/O pin, but it is still a reset input at boot: do not hold it low while powering up (WOLLE-MINIEVB)","Sketches that use the watchdog or sleep modes need changes (WOLLE-LGT)","USB power passes a protection diode, so the 5V rail is about 4.6 V on USB (WOLLE-LGT)(WOLLE-MINIEVB)","Regulator: AMS1117 (the board in the lgt8fx photo reads 5.0); the lgt8fx wiki lists a 3.3 V version too. Read the regulator marking and measure the 5V pin before trusting 5 V logic (LGT8FX-WIKI-NANO)(LGT8FX-NANO-PHOTO)","LQFP48 and SSOP20 MiniEVB boards have different pins and are not covered by this table (WOLLE-MINIEVB)"],
