    "notes": ["Header order: Random Nerd Tutorials' pinout drawing; the V1.6 schematic's P1/P2 nets agree. Ai-Thinker's own docs could not be opened (RNT-CAM-IMG)(CAM-SCH)","No USB socket: program through U0R/U0T with a 3.3 V USB-serial adapter, holding IO0 to GND while resetting; remove that link to run the program (RNT-CAM)","Power through the 5V pin; many people report errors when powering it from 3.3 V (RNT-CAM)","The microSD slot uses IO2, IO4, IO12, IO13, IO14 and IO15; without a card they are free, and 1-bit SD mode frees IO12 and IO13 (RNT-CAM)","IO4 is both the flash LED and SD DATA1, so the flash lights during card access unless SD runs in 1-bit mode (RNT-CAM)","Small red LED on GPIO33 (not on the header), lit when GPIO33 is LOW (RNT-CAM)","Camera uses GPIO0, 5, 18, 19, 21, 22, 23, 25, 26, 27, 32 (power-down), 34, 35, 36 and 39 internally (RNT-CAM)","Every free header GPIO is on ADC2, which the Wi-Fi driver also uses, so analog reads can fail while Wi-Fi is on (IDF-ADC)","ESP32-CAM-MB USB base: CH340-series USB-serial chip (install the CH340 driver) with RST and IO0 buttons; if auto-upload fails, hold IO0 on the base and tap RST on the ESP32-CAM itself (RNT-CAM-MB)","Header pin-to-signal mapping matches the V1.6 schematic: P2 = 5V, GND, IO12, IO13, IO15, IO14, IO2, IO4; P1 = 3V3, IO16, IO0, GND, VCC, U0RXD, U0TXD, GND (CAM-SCH)","Some boards print GND/R on the last right-hand pad (the one next to U0T): it is wired to reset by default. Use the GND next to IO0 as ground. (MAKERGUIDES-CAM)(ARD-FORUM-CAM-GNDR)"],
    "sources": [{"title":"RNT-CAM: Random Nerd Tutorials, ESP32-CAM AI-Thinker Pinout Guide: GPIOs Usage Explained (gave the header order)","url":"https://randomnerdtutorials.com/esp32-cam-ai-thinker-pinout/"},{"title":"RNT-CAM-IMG: Random Nerd Tutorials ESP32-CAM pinout drawing (image used for the header order)","url":"https://i0.wp.com/randomnerdtutorials.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/ESP32-CAM-pinout-new.png"},{"title":"CAM-SCH: ESP32-CAM V1.6 schematic (PDF linked by RNT, hosted in SeeedDocument/forum_doc)","url":"https://github.com/SeeedDocument/forum_doc/blob/master/reg/ESP32_CAM_V1.6.pdf"},{"title":"RNT-CAM-MB: Random Nerd Tutorials, Upload Code to ESP32-CAM AI-Thinker using ESP32-CAM-MB USB Programmer","url":"https://randomnerdtutorials.com/upload-code-esp32-cam-mb-usb/"},{"title":"IDF-ADC: ESP-IDF Programming Guide (ESP32), Analog to Digital Converter Oneshot Mode Driver, Hardware Limitations","url":"https://docs.espressif.com/projects/esp-idf/en/latest/esp32/api-reference/peripherals/adc/adc_oneshot.html"},{"title":"ESP32-DS: Espressif ESP32 Series Datasheet v5.3 (pin list, input-only GPIO34-39, strapping pins GPIO0/2/5/12/15)","url":"https://www.espressif.com/sites/default/files/documentation/esp32_datasheet_en.pdf"}],
    "header_order_source": "RNT-CAM pinout drawing (silkscreen labels on the board render) for physical order; CAM-SCH P1/P2 header nets agree pin for pin. Ai-Thinker's own docs page (docs.ai-thinker.com) returned 403 Forbidden, so it was not read."
