    "notes": ["Header order: Espressif's J1/J3 tables, placed with Espressif's pin layout image (J1 left, pin 1 at the antenna end) (ESP-S3-GUIDE)(ESP-S3-PINLAYOUT)","Two Micro-USB ports: 'UART' goes through the USB-to-UART bridge to TX/RX (GPIO43/44); 'USB' is the chip's own full-speed USB on GPIO19/20, also usable for flashing and JTAG (ESP-S3-GUIDE)","Power from one source only: USB port(s), or 5V and G pins, or 3V3 and G pins (ESP-S3-GUIDE)","RGB LED is on GPIO38 on v1.1 boards and on GPIO48 on the initial version (ESP-S3-GUIDE)","N16R8 (and N32R16V) modules use octal PSRAM/flash, which takes GPIO35, 36 and 37; N8R2 has quad PSRAM, so those pins stay free (ESP-S3-GUIDE)(S3-WROOM1-DS)","Espressif sold this board as DevKitC-1-N8R2 (now end of life) and -N16R8; AliExpress copies were not checked against any source, so compare their printed labels with this table (ESP-S3-GUIDE)","Download mode: hold BOOT (GPIO0) and press RST; GPIO46 must stay LOW (its default) (S3-DS)","UART, SPI and I2C signals can be routed to almost any GPIO through the GPIO matrix; the FSPI labels are the fixed fast-path pins (S3-DS)","Every GPIO pin carries the PWM mark on Espressif's pin layout (ESP-S3-PINLAYOUT)"],
