    "notes": ["\"bottom\" lists the 4-pin SWD header (silk SW) at the end away from USB, left to right in this view (WEACT-PINOUT)(WEACT-SCH)","Header order is the same on V2.0, V3.0 and V3.1 (V3.1 notes 'pin definition unchanged'); V2.0 prints '3.3' where later boards print '3V3' (WEACT-SHAPE)(WEACT-HW)","Genuine boards carry the 'WeAct Studio' logo and a version number; WeAct says boards without both are not made by them (WEACT-README)","Chips: F401CC 84 MHz, 256 KB flash, 64 KB RAM; F401CE 84 MHz, 512 KB, 96 KB (both discontinued); F411CE 100 MHz, 512 KB, 128 KB (WEACT-README)","F411: PA0 and PB5 are standard 3.3 V I/O (TC); all other header GPIOs are 5 V tolerant (FT) (ST-F411-DS)","F401: all I/O ports are 5 V tolerant (FT) (ST-F401-DS)","FT pins are not 5 V tolerant in analog mode, nor PC14/PC15 in oscillator mode (ST-F411-DS)(ST-F401-DS)","PC13-PC15 sink only about 3 mA, max 2 MHz, and must not source current (e.g. to drive an LED) (ST-F411-DS)(ST-F401-DS)","LEDs: red power LED; blue user LED from 3.3 V through 1.5 kohm into PC13, so it lights when PC13 is low (WEACT-SCH)","KEY button: PA0 to GND through 330 ohm, no external pull-up on the schematic (KEY added in V1.3, 330 ohm in V3.0) (WEACT-SCH)(WEACT-HW)","ROM bootloader (ISP): hold BOOT0, press and release NRST, release BOOT0 about 0.5 s later; then flash over USB-C (DFU) or a USB-serial adapter on PA9/PA10 with STM32CubeProgrammer (WEACT-README)","If DFU is not recognised, WeAct suggests warming the chip slightly (to about 25 C) and entering ISP mode again (WEACT-README)","System-memory bootloader interfaces include USART1 (PA9/PA10) and USB OTG FS DFU (PA11/PA12) (ST-F411-DS)","WeAct HID bootloader (if installed): hold KEY while powering up or resetting; the C13 LED blinks (WEACT-README)","Footprint for an optional user-fitted SPI flash (W25Qxx): CS PA4, SCK PA5, MISO PA6, MOSI PA7; V2.0 moved flash MISO to PB4, V2.1 moved it back to PA6 (WEACT-SCH)(WEACT-HW)","5V pin is USB VBUS through diode D4 (V2.2+); V3.1 adds solder bridge SB1 to bypass it for USB-host 5 V output (WEACT-SCH)(WEACT-HW)","V3.1 regulator is ME6231A33M3G: 3-18 V operating input, 500 mA max output, SOT23-3 (WEACT-HW)(ME6231-DS)","VB feeds VBAT (RTC backup) through a BAT54C dual diode shared with 3.3 V (WEACT-SCH)","32.768 kHz and 25 MHz crystals are fitted (WEACT-README)(WEACT-SCH)"],
    "sources": [{"title":"WEACT-README: WeActStudio.MiniSTM32F4x1 README (STM32F4x1 MiniF4)","url":"https://github.com/WeActStudio/WeActStudio.MiniSTM32F4x1"},{"title":"WEACT-HW: WeActStudio.MiniSTM32F4x1 Hardware release notes (V1.2-V3.1)","url":"https://github.com/WeActStudio/WeActStudio.MiniSTM32F4x1/blob/master/Hardware/README.md"},{"title":"WEACT-SHAPE: WeAct STM32F4x1 V3.0 and V2.0+ board shape drawings","url":"https://github.com/WeActStudio/WeActStudio.MiniSTM32F4x1/blob/master/images/STM32F4x1_V30_BoardShape.png"},{"title":"WEACT-PINOUT: STM32F4x1Cx v2.0+ Pinout Diagram (Richard Balint, in WeAct repo; PDF version in General document/)","url":"https://github.com/WeActStudio/WeActStudio.MiniSTM32F4x1/blob/master/images/STM32F4x1_PinoutDiagram_RichardBalint.png"},{"title":"WEACT-SCH: MiniF4x1Cx V3.1 schematic (WeAct Studio, 2021-04-17)","url":"https://github.com/WeActStudio/WeActStudio.MiniSTM32F4x1/blob/master/Hardware/MiniF4x1Cx_V31%20SchDoc.pdf"},{"title":"ST-F411-DS: STMicroelectronics STM32F411xC/xE datasheet, DocID026289 Rev 7 (copy in WeAct repo; st.com refused automated download)","url":"https://github.com/WeActStudio/WeActStudio.MiniSTM32F4x1/blob/master/Datasheet/STM32F411CEU6_Datasheet.pdf"},{"title":"ST-F401-DS: STMicroelectronics STM32F401xD/xE datasheet, DocID025644 Rev 3 (copy in WeAct repo)","url":"https://github.com/WeActStudio/WeActStudio.MiniSTM32F4x1/blob/master/Datasheet/STM32F401CEU6_Datasheet.pdf"},{"title":"ME6231-DS: Microne ME6231 series 18 V LDO datasheet (copy in WeAct repo)","url":"https://github.com/WeActStudio/WeActStudio.MiniSTM32F4x1/blob/master/Datasheet/ME6231A33M3G.PDF"}],
