    "notes": ["Header order: Waveshare's wiki pinout image, matching its schematic (WS-PINOUT)(WS-SCH)","Castellated pads on three edges: 9 down each side plus 5 along the bottom edge; \"bottom\" lists those 5 left to right (WS-PINOUT)","Underside: a column of 10 small pads (bottom view, USB at the top, column near the right edge), from the USB end: GND, GP25, GP24, GP23, GP22, GP21, GP20, GP19, GP18, GP17 (WS-PINOUT)","Underside pad functions: GP17 SPI0 CSn / I2C0 SCL / UART0 RX; GP18 SPI0 SCK / I2C1 SDA; GP19 SPI0 TX / I2C1 SCL; GP20 I2C0 SDA; GP21 I2C0 SCL; GP22-GP25 plain GPIO (WS-PINOUT)","GP16 is not on any pad: it drives the onboard WS2812B RGB LED (DIN), which runs from 3.3 V (WS-PINOUT)(WS-SCH)","Every GPIO can do PWM and PIO (WS-PINOUT)","BOOT button pulls the flash chip-select (QSPI_SS) low through 1 kohm; RESET button pulls RUN low (WS-SCH)","To flash: hold BOOT, press and release RESET, then release BOOT (or hold BOOT while plugging in USB); a USB drive appears; copy a .uf2 file onto it (WS-WIKI)","5V pad is VSYS, wired straight to USB VBUS with no diode; Waveshare says add a diode if feeding a battery into it; there is no charger or battery protection (WS-WIKI)(WS-SCH)","3.3 V comes from an RT9013-33 LDO (2.2-5.5 V operating input), so keep the 5V pad at 5.5 V or less (WS-SCH)(RT9013-PAGE)","A 3.3 V battery or supply can go straight to the 3V3 pad, per Waveshare (WS-WIKI)","No SWD debug pins are brought out; Waveshare says debugging on this board is not possible (WS-WIKI)","ADC reference is the 3.3 V rail through 200 ohm; there is no ADC_VREF pad (WS-SCH)","RP2040 GPIO absolute maximum is IOVDD + 0.5 V (IOVDD max 3.63 V): not 5 V tolerant (RP2040-DS)","Genuine boards carry the Waveshare logo; Waveshare warns of copies built with low-quality parts (WS-WIKI)"],
